Add a BlockSignatureStrategy that skips only the block signature.

Differential testing runs every client with validate_result = false, which in
pyspec terms means the block signature and the post-state root are not checked
while RANDAO and attestation signatures still are. Upstream offers no strategy
with that shape: VerifyBulk and VerifyIndividual check everything, and
NoVerification checks nothing, so a client running under it accepts blocks whose
RANDAO reveal is wrong and disagrees with pyspec on exactly the cases this
project is looking for.

SkipBlockSignatureOnly maps to VerifySignatures::True so the per-operation
verification stays on, and the one call it has to suppress -- verify_block_signature
-- is guarded on the strategy itself.
diff --git a/consensus/state_processing/src/per_block_processing.rs b/consensus/state_processing/src/per_block_processing.rs
index 99abbef..28dcb1a 100644
--- a/consensus/state_processing/src/per_block_processing.rs
+++ b/consensus/state_processing/src/per_block_processing.rs
@@ -61,6 +61,8 @@ pub enum BlockSignatureStrategy {
     VerifyRandao,
     /// Verify all signatures in bulk at the beginning of block processing.
     VerifyBulk,
+    /// Skip block signature verification only, but verify all other signatures (RANDAO, attestations, etc.)
+    SkipBlockSignatureOnly,
 }
 
 /// The strategy to be used when validating the block's signatures.
@@ -144,6 +146,10 @@ pub fn per_block_processing<E: EthSpec, Payload: AbstractExecPayload<E>>(
         BlockSignatureStrategy::VerifyIndividual => VerifySignatures::True,
         BlockSignatureStrategy::NoVerification => VerifySignatures::False,
         BlockSignatureStrategy::VerifyRandao => VerifySignatures::False,
+        BlockSignatureStrategy::SkipBlockSignatureOnly => {
+            // validate_result = false: Skip block signature, but verify other signatures
+            VerifySignatures::True
+        }
     };
 
     let proposer_index = process_block_header(
@@ -154,7 +160,8 @@ pub fn per_block_processing<E: EthSpec, Payload: AbstractExecPayload<E>>(
         spec,
     )?;
 
-    if verify_signatures.is_true() {
+    // validate_result = false: Skip block signature verification when SkipBlockSignatureOnly
+    if verify_signatures.is_true() && block_signature_strategy != BlockSignatureStrategy::SkipBlockSignatureOnly {
         verify_block_signature(state, signed_block, ctxt, spec)?;
     }
 
